{"name":"Safari Vest","hex":"#b2a68f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"},{"term":"vest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment that buttons down the front, worn over a shirt, and often as part of a suit; a waistcoat.","A sleeveless garment, often with a low-cut neck, usually worn under a shirt or blouse."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clothe with, or as with, a vestment, or garment; to dress; to robe; to cover, surround, or encompass closely.","To clothe with authority, power, etc.; to put in possession; to invest; to furnish; to endow; followed by with and the thing conferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ernest Hemingway posing with a Cape buffalo he shot on a safari hunt in Africa in the early 1950s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErnest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg/330px-Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg/330px-Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man in safari gear in the early 1900s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg"}],"sounds":{"safari":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-safari.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/67/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-safari.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-safari.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/67/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-safari.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-safari.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-safari.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-safari.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-safari.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-safari